verdicts.evidence:
THEOREM (C1-8, restated with the hypotheses the probe needed).
Hypotheses:
- L = Π L_c is a product of finite-height lattices with join merges;
- F = ⊔ f_p, with each f_p monotone;
- E1: each f_p reads only its declared inputs and paths;
- E2: no self-clearing fire-once; E5: no truncation by fuel or contradiction mid-round;
- W₀ ⊇ {p : f_p(x⁰) ⋢ x⁰}.
Define G(h)(0) = x⁰ and G(h)(n+1) = x⁰ ⊔ F(h(n)). Let c(h)(n) = ⊔_{m≤n} h(m), the sparse 'inherit' read.
Claims:
- (i) G's unique fixpoint is the Kleene sequence K;
- (ii) lfp(c∘G) = K, because K is increasing and F is monotone;
- (iii) any fair chaotic iteration that re-evaluates p̂ at depth d whenever an input of p changes at a depth ≤ d reaches K (Üresin–Dubois; Cousot RR-88, applied to the components (c, d));
- (iv) every (p, d) at which an input of p changes must be evaluated at least once. That set is exactly BSP's fire set from (x⁰, W₀), and BSP's round order attains it.
Without E1, (iii) fails: an undeclared read is not a dependency, so a late arrival does not re-fire. Without joins, the closure is not a join.
MEASUREMENT (`timeout -k 10 120 "/Applications/Racket v9.3/bin/racket" w29-lifted-kleene.rkt`, real propagator.rkt).
Soundness:
- 7 join fixtures (chain-6, fan-in-4, X3 cycle, diamond, a climbing 2-cycle at H = 8 / 16 / 32);
- × BSP and drain schedules × forward and reverse install;
- × lift modes {declared deps + depth view, declared deps + latest view, all deps + depth view};
- every run equals Kleene per depth and BSP's rounds.
Cost, in evaluations of the original fire:
- climb, BSP fires 18 / 34 / 66: stateless lift 90 / 306 / 1 122 on the depth-ordered schedule and 126 / 442 / 1 650 on the drain (O(D²), because a stateless lifted fire re-evaluates every breakpoint);
- X3: 12 against 24–33; chain-6: 11 against 16–21;
- all-deps mode: 12–3 506.
Storage equals BSP's round content (66 stored (cell, depth) entries against 66 changes).
There is no stateless O(D) realization. One propagator per depth creates propagators during S0, which G-1 forbids, and its bound N is Σ heights, which is not computable (SC-19). Remembering the last depth processed is state outside cells.
Under hypothesis failure:
- F5b (E1 fails; the undeclared cell changes at the same depth): BSP o = 5 under both install orders, equal to Kleene. DIRECT stand-in, reverse order: o = 1. The declared-deps lift gives o = 5 in three schedules and o = 1 on drain-reverse, the same as DIRECT's wrong answer, so the lifted oracle is blind exactly there. The BSP replay flags it.
- F7 (non-join cell, two same-depth writers): BSP gives f = a or b, by install order. The all-deps lift exhausted its fuel at 10⁶ lifted fires (livelock).
- F5 (C5's K-UR): only all-deps lifts reach the lfp, at 6–10× the evaluations.

defence.design_that_would_make_it_pay:
Information flow, not steps. P0.5 gains two items, pinned together as B-P05′:
- the thread executor off (O-14);
- the keyed diff for pointwise merges, inside net-cell-write, with W2-2's equivalence monitor and its drop-a-key power row.
P2's S0 executor:
- a set-worklist loop over the live persistent network, writing through net-cell-write's merge;
- fire-once as a grow-only fired set held by the scheduler, consulted at dequeue, with productive = trigger held (CL-7). Dependents are never pruned in S0; pruning becomes a topology action at the boundary or disappears;
- the Tier-1 branch deleted (PD-2 fixed by deletion), and the drain retired onto K = 1;
- no write log anywhere.
The BSP oracle:
- replays from (x⁰ₑ, W₀) (C5-4); x⁰ₑ is a pointer at K = 1;
- compares the union of both runs' changed sets (C7-4);
- carries the merge-order census, moved into the replay (C7-4);
- uses executor mutants as power rows (drop one enqueue; skip one latch);
- gives rounds lazily per epoch, with RM-1 measured on the LSP path.
P2's gate, semantic first:
- replay: 0 differences on converted cells;
- R2: DIRECT keeps the serializable result;
- C5's T1: fixpoint reached;
- the E1 census at 0, with its five power rows as tests;
- performance against B-P05′ from W2-2's instrument, not 1.4× against B-P05.
Fenced cells keep K = 1 DIRECT's semantics (CL-4 option (i)): a BSP sub-run at K > 1 loses R2's update (W2-9-2).
The lifted network is not built; its theorem goes into D.3 §5.

findings.evidence:
An injected executor fires each pid normally, then re-fires it against perturbed copies of the same snapshot and compares the fire's contribution. The contribution is the changed component paths with their values, or the post value for non-map outputs. Levels:
- L0: the same snapshot (statelessness);
- L1: every non-declared cell that is some propagator's output, poisoned;
- L3: every non-declared cell poisoned;
- LP: inside path-declared map inputs, every component neither watched nor written, poisoned. Changes at poisoned paths are excluded, because they are the merge reading poison.
Power rows (`… w29-e1-census.rkt POWER`): undeclared cell read → L1 1, L3 1; declared-only → 0 everywhere; undeclared path read → LP-raised 1, or LP 1 without a raise; impure box counter → L0 1.
Corpus: `for f in benchmarks/comparative/*.prologos; do timeout -k 10 90 racket w29-e1-census.rkt $f; done`. Across 12 files with S0 fires: L0 0 / 2 901, L1 0 / 2 901, L3 0 / 2 901, LP 0 / 2 815, LP-raised 0. Rounds and fires are identical between the control and the census legs (e.g. 214 / 1 136, 185 / 1 140), so the census did not perturb the runs.
Other files:
- six files had no Tier-2 BSP rounds;
- parity-adversarial raises 'solve: Depth limit exceeded (100)' under plain process-file with both executors (w29-parity-control.out), so it is unmeasured.
Instrument correction: my first LP version flagged 70 / 65 fires at typing-propagators.rkt:1841 (make-app-fire-fn). Those were merge artefacts at written-but-unchanged paths, and the exclusion removed them.
